=== P2 Shared surface 0060 AIWatchFaceNLResponse (Windows) ===

Surface: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/AIWatchFaceNLResponse.{Model,Source,ViewModel}.cs + .cs (view)
Tests:   apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/AIWatchFaceNLResponseTests.cs
Web src: web/src/components/ai/AIWatchFaceNLResponse.tsx (THE specification)

Parity port of the web AIWatchFaceNLResponse composed with its shared AIFeatureCard scaffold and the
withAiFeature gate. Opt-in Helix narrator on the /watch route that answers glance-style natural-language
questions about the install's primary vehicle. The action POSTs an OPTIONAL { message } body to
/api/v1/ai/watch/respond via the canonical useAiStream SSE contract and streams the narration into the output
region. An empty question is allowed — the body serialises to {} and the backend applies its deterministic
glance-summary default prompt. The deterministic /watch fixed cards + tap-command surface remain the canonical
baseline (ADR-015 §I3 + §I5 + §I6); this is the opt-in narration section layered beneath them, and renders
NOTHING when the feature is off.

Data sources (web): useTranslation, useAiStream.
Shared components (web -> native): AIFeatureCard scaffold, withAiFeature gate, ui Textarea -> the native
glass-card composition (PanelTitle + Helix TsBadge + description + TsTextarea + universal "Ask Helix" TsButton +
streamed output region). No charts / maps in this surface.

Architecture (mirrors the shipped AIRAGHelp narrate-with-textarea surface, the closest analogue — same
useTranslation + useAiStream + AIFeatureCard + withAiFeature + Textarea import set). Each AI shared surface owns
its own stream stack; only IAiFeatureGate is shared. This surface uses the AiWatch* prefix:
  - .Model.cs       : AIWatchFaceNLResponseRegistration (FeatureId/Slug/RootAutomationId/RespondPath +
                      MaxMessageChars=1000 + the six web i18n keys with catalog-verified fallbacks),
                      AiWatchStreamState / AiWatchEventKind / AiWatchErrorReason, AiWatchStreamEvent,
                      AiWatchRequest (optional `message`, snake-pinned, JsonIgnore WhenWritingNull so an empty
                      question serialises to {}), AiWatchSseParser (native port of useAiStream
                      parseSSEFrame/toTypedEvent), AIWatchFaceNLResponseDiagnostics.
  - .Source.cs      : IAiWatchStreamTransport (P1/S8 seam) + HttpAiWatchStreamTransport (POSTs the body, reads
                      text/event-stream, classifies HTTP vs Network failure). Reuses the shared IAiFeatureGate /
                      StaticAiFeatureGate / DelegateAiFeatureGate (canonical home:
                      AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative.Source.cs).
  - .ViewModel.cs   : UI-thread-free state holder. Gate (IsGateOpen), the canStart guard
                      (CanStart = MessageWithinCap (trimmed length <= MaxMessageChars) AND state != paused-confirm
                      — an EMPTY question is allowed), the useAiStream lifecycle (idle -> streaming -> done/error,
                      duplicate-start no-op, cancel -> idle), offline classification, the optional-message
                      request body, and all projected labels. No HTTP, no WinUI types.
  - .cs (view)      : WinUI 3 ContentControl. Tokenized glass Border card -> header (PanelTitle + Helix TsBadge +
                      wrapped description) + TsTextarea (MinHeight rows=3, MaxLength=1000, accessible name from
                      watchFaceNL.inputLabel) + right-aligned universal "Ask Helix" TsButton -> output region
                      (TsSkeleton thinking / Text narration / offline-aware FontIcon+Text error). withAiFeature
                      gate collapses the whole surface (Visibility.Collapsed + cleared automation id) when off.

States rendered (on-demand SSE action — there is no cached prior result to age, so no "stale" state, matching the
web hook's stream_http_* -> error fallback and the shipped AIRAGHelp sibling): gate-off (collapsed) - idle
(output region hidden, card always visible) - streaming/thinking skeleton - accumulating narration text -
error / offline (connectivity-aware message). Every branch is asserted headlessly in the view-model per-state
tests (the headless snapshot of what the view renders in each state).

i18n: every string resolves through the ILocalizer facade (P1/S10). The six web keys
(watchFaceNL.{title,description,button,badge,placeholder,inputLabel}) are present in
apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw (verified — translation.watchFaceNL.* at L20526-20541); the registration
fallbacks are the web second-arg copy verbatim. The shared helix.* CTA keys (helix.askHelix / helix.thinking)
and ai.common.errorUnknown / common.offline are consumed exactly as the shipped AIRAGHelp sibling consumes them
(catalog value when present, English fallback otherwise — they originate in the AIFeatureCard scaffold bundle,
out of scope here). No English literals in the view.

Accessibility: Narrator name on the card and the badge; the question field carries its own accessible name
(watchFaceNL.inputLabel "Your question for Helix", the web textarea aria-label); the action button carries the
composed "Ask Helix \u00b7 Ask about my car" accessible name + the per-feature verb tooltip; thinking skeleton
honours MotionPreference.ReduceMotion; streamed output uses a LiveRegion so Narrator announces deltas; input is
hard-capped at MaxMessageChars so an over-cap parser-rejection 400 can never reach the user.

Telemetry: AIWatchFaceNLResponseDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=AIWatchFaceNLResponse" (PII-safe — never the
question text, the narration, the vehicle id, or token usage) once when the surface is shown (P1/S11).

Hook-URL verification (acceptance): RespondPath "/ai/watch/respond" matches the backend route
internal/api/ai_routes.go:690  r.Post("/watch/respond", g.Wrap("watch-face-nl-response", watchFaceNLResponseHandler))
(mounted under the /ai group, +/api/v1 prefix => /api/v1/ai/watch/respond). The Go handler decodes the optional
`message` field (internal/api/aiwatchnl/handler_test.go POSTs {"message":"..."}), confirming the wire field name.
Feature id "watch-face-nl-response" is present in AiFeatureRegistry.Features (verified by test) and in the web
registry web/src/ai/features.ts.

